id: pm-j668gl
title: "The Windows nightly leg cannot separate product defects from harness noise: 744 hardcoded POSIX path literals and 203 raw errno strings in the suite fail on Windows for reasons unrelated to pm behaviour"
description: "GH-791 (windows-latest / Node 24, commit d885d5a0) fails four tests. Exactly one of them is a product defect - the merge-safety workspace_root canonicalization tracked as pm-ihmfs6, which also fails on macOS. The other three are properties of the suite, not of pm:\n\n1. tests/unit/sdk/merge-safety.spec.ts 'installs idempotent git attributes/config and exercises the CLI adapter' - same path-spelling family as pm-ihmfs6.\n2. tests/unit/packages/guide-shell-runtime.spec.ts 'builds completion registries and list helpers across schema shapes' - asserts listAllItemMetadata was called with the literal '/tmp/pm' (lines 24, 28, 120, 136, 142). On Windows path.resolve('/tmp/pm') is C:\\tmp\\pm, so the assertion cannot hold and never could.\n3. tests/unit/sdk/context-integrity-primitives.spec.ts 'invalidates derived drift state after conventional history writes' - asserts the warning string history_drift_cache_invalidation_failed:ENOTDIR. Windows raises a different errno for the same condition. This one has a product tail worth deciding separately: the diagnostic code embeds a raw platform errno, so the warning an agent parses is platform-dependent.\n\nCensus of the class across tests/: 744 hardcoded POSIX absolute path literals matching \"/(tmp|home|var|usr)/ in 81 files (worst: extension-loader.spec.ts 159, search-command.spec.ts 137, extensions-runtime.spec.ts 48, builtin-extension-entrypoints.spec.ts 39, telemetry-runtime.spec.ts 34, settings-store.spec.ts 30), plus 203 raw errno literals.\n\nWhy this matters more than tidiness: the Windows leg has been red often enough (pm-e70zh5 records a 32/84 scheduled-run failure rate) that a red leg carries no information. Today it is red for one real cross-platform defect and three artifacts, and nothing in the failure output distinguishes them - somebody has to read four stack traces to learn that. The suite is asserting on the harness's temp-directory conventions rather than on pm, so a genuine Windows regression would arrive already camouflaged.\n\nRemedy: route path literals through the existing helpers (withTempPmPath, mockPosixPath) or path.join from os.tmpdir(), and assert on normalized error classes rather than raw errno strings. Prefer a lint rule or a gate over a one-time sweep, since the count grows with every new spec."
type: Chore
status: open
priority: 2
tags[5]: ci,cross-platform,nightly,test-quality,windows
created_at: "2026-07-28T10:29:33.965Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-30T17:16:27.243Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: No test asserts on a hardcoded POSIX absolute path or a raw platform errno string; a red Windows nightly leg names only product defects
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
