comments[17]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T11:53:13.607Z","harness:codex","Progress tranche evidence: canonical/native path expectations were fixed in merge safety, guide-shell runtime, and context-integrity tests, and drift-cache filesystem failures now expose stable diagnostic codes instead of raw errno text. The full repo-wide removal of all hardcoded POSIX paths and raw errno assertions remains, so this broader chore returns to open after the cross-platform nightly evidence is captured on pm-ihmfs6."
  "2026-07-28T11:57:10.427Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/795 at implementation head 862e88f71. The PR description links canonical PM records and records full coverage, isolated consumer, security, compatibility, and token-gate evidence."
  "2026-07-28T12:15:00.058Z","harness:codex","Nightly run 30356894804 reduced the Windows failures to three actionable portability cases: stable diagnostic semantics for invalid tracker roots, one canonical-path assertion, and cwd-safe cleanup. Implemented deterministic root classification independent of raw errno, realpath expectations, and finally-guarded cwd restoration; focused 27 tests and strict static quality now pass."
  "2026-07-28T12:30:36.407Z","harness:codex","Nightly evidence: run 30358494567 completed with Ubuntu Node 22/24/25 and macOS Node 24 green; Windows Node 24 exposed two deterministic cross-platform test gaps after 6,445 tests passed: missing-cache ENOENT masked an invalid tracker-root diagnostic, and merge-driver assertions assumed POSIX separators. Fixing both under this actively claimed Windows portability tranche; no product regression was hidden or waived."
  "2026-07-28T12:42:49.553Z","harness:codex","Nightly run 30359443098 confirmed the native-separator assertions are fixed: Windows advanced to 6,446 passing tests with one remaining invalid-root diagnostic failure. The Windows filesystem accepted a non-canonical composite tracker spelling during stat classification, so root validity is now established through realpath before directory inspection; the gate remains strict and the item remains actively owned."
  "2026-07-28T12:53:08.296Z","harness:codex","Root-cause refinement from run 30360194405: on Windows, fs.rm({force:true}) may treat a cache path beneath a non-directory ancestor as an already-missing success, so post-error classification cannot run. The primitive now validates the canonical tracker root before removal and tests both a file root and an unreachable descendant; valid missing-cache removal remains a quiet success."
  "2026-07-28T13:04:23.670Z","harness:codex","Completed tranche evidence: run 30361026722 is green on Windows Node 24 after canonical merge paths, native separator assertions, cwd-safe cleanup, and stable drift-cache diagnostics. The acceptance criterion is intentionally broader than this delivery: the repo-wide POSIX-literal/raw-errno census remains, so this item returns to open and is released rather than falsely closed."
  "2026-07-28T15:18:48.550Z","harness:claude-code","Cross-platform nightly is GREEN on main again, verified by dispatch 2026-07-28. Run 30372071932 on main succeeded in 7m31s with every leg passing, immediately after PR#795 merged at 14:20:36Z.\n\nThe preceding red streak was pre-fix, not an unowned regression: the last three scheduled runs on main failed (30334992958 at 06:29Z today, 30246735868 on 07-27, 30191427127 on 07-26), all on the same two legs, macos-latest Node 24 and windows-latest Node 24, and the actual failures were four specs — guide-shell-runtime building completion registries across schema shapes, context-integrity-primitives invalidating derived drift state after conventional history writes, and merge-safety twice for installing idempotent git attributes and for preferring explicit tracker paths over protected source coordinates. Every scheduled run predated the merge, and PR#795's own branch was named for this work and had already been verified by dispatch, run 30361026722 passing at 12:54Z.\n\nThe durable lesson for this item rather than the incident: a scheduled-only signal necessarily reports a stale verdict for as long as the interval, so a red nightly on main is not evidence of a live defect until the last completed run postdates the last merge. Confirm by dispatch before filing anything, and compare the run start against the merge timestamp rather than against the calendar day."
  "2026-07-29T14:21:32.894Z","harness:codex","Progress evidence for GH-810 tranche: workspace snapshot server cleanup now checks listening state before close, preserving the original listen failure while eliminating Windows cleanup noise. Focused snapshot/test-command tests and full 6510-test exact-coverage suite pass on Linux; the broader portability census remains open pending the new PR nightly Windows run."
  "2026-07-29T14:33:11.026Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/811 at implementation head 51478084e; description links canonical PM records and records exact coverage, packed-consumer, security, changelog, and same-day release-guard evidence."
  "2026-07-29T17:04:46.351Z","harness:claude-code","Nightly leg status enumerated 2026-07-29. The scheduled run at 06:34 UTC, run id 30428599608, failed. Exactly one leg is red: Nightly on windows-latest with Node 24. Every other leg in the matrix succeeded.\n\nTwo specs fail on that leg and no others:\n\ntests/unit/commands/test-command.spec.ts, runTest, \"terminates stubborn timed-out linked commands without hanging\" - failed after 3,693 ms, which is the timeout itself rather than an assertion. This one is a product-behaviour candidate, not spec noise: if a stubborn child cannot be killed on Windows, linked-test timeout enforcement does not work there, and the precedent in this class is explicit that the fix must not be spec-side only.\n\ntests/unit/sdk/workspace-snapshot.spec.ts, workspace snapshots, \"rejects non-file filesystem entries in authoritative state\" - failed in 93 ms, an assertion failure on filesystem-entry classification. This is on the snapshot surface that shipped on 2026-07-28, so the class is still acquiring new members as new surfaces land, which is the argument for the portability sweep this item owns rather than another point patch.\n\nVerification state. The auto-filed leg issue was closed on 2026-07-29 and the 2026-07-29 lanes merged afterwards, so no scheduled nightly has run against current HEAD. A dispatch was queued at 17:01 UTC, run id 30473431691, to establish whether HEAD is green independently of the closure. Do not treat the issue closure as evidence of a green leg.\n"
  "2026-07-29T17:10:59.941Z","harness:claude-code","Dispatch verdict for the run queued earlier this session: run id 30473431691 against main at commit c66cb7ca8, completed failure at 17:09 UTC.\n\nFour of five legs are green - ubuntu with Node 22, 24 and 25, and macos with Node 24. windows-latest with Node 24 is red and it is now a single-spec residual:\n\ntests/unit/sdk/workspace-snapshot.spec.ts, workspace snapshots, \"rejects non-file filesystem entries in authoritative state\", assertion failure in 102 ms.\n\nThe other spec that failed on the 06:34 scheduled run, the linked-command termination timeout in tests/unit/commands/test-command.spec.ts, passes against current HEAD. So the 2026-07-29 lanes fixed one of the two and the leg issue was closed one failure early.\n\nTwo things this settles. First, the leg is genuinely red against HEAD with no open GitHub issue tracking it, because the auto-filing path runs on the scheduled trigger only - this item is the tracking of record. Second, the surviving failure is on the workspace snapshot surface that shipped 2026-07-28, in the same spec file that the restore-durability item pm-6l2mza links as its verification target, so the portability fix and the durability fix will touch the same file and should be sequenced rather than raced.\n"
  "2026-07-29T18:28:08.216Z","harness:codex","Active tranche evidence: the snapshot authoritative-state test now skips only the Unix-domain-socket construction on Windows, where binding that path is unsupported, while retaining real non-file socket rejection coverage on Unix. The complete 6,528-test suite passes with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage on this checkout. The broad repository-wide portability census remains larger than this tranche and will be returned to open pending the PR Windows nightly result."
  "2026-07-29T18:51:21.783Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR for the snapshot portability tranche: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/813 at implementation head c7ac2767e. The item remains open and unclaimed because its repo-wide POSIX-path/raw-errno census is intentionally broader; PR Windows evidence will be appended after the exact-head runner completes."
  "2026-07-29T19:59:29.265Z","harness:codex","PR #813 implementation evidence for the open, released census: the representative and scratch corpus benchmark paths now run sequentially, remove obsolete numeric tiers, share SDK-generated identities, tolerate valueless shape input deterministically, and publish measured profiles without retaining full populations. This advances the portability census without claiming the broader cross-platform corpus complete. Exact-tree gates pass, including 6530 tests and 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-07-29T20:15:19.358Z","harness:codex","Lineage correction for PR #813: the preceding 2026-07-29T19:59 corpus benchmark comment was associated with this Windows portability chore in error and must not be interpreted as progress toward its path/errno portability acceptance criteria. The corpus-shape generator, comparison, and benchmark evidence belongs to canonical item pm-vv2lti, where those files and tests are linked. This append-only correction supersedes only that misplaced claim; the valid snapshot socket portability evidence and broader open census status remain unchanged."
  "2026-07-30T17:16:27.243Z","harness:claude-code","Nightly signal at HEAD, 2026-07-30 (evening). Dispatched a nightly run at 87d88c5e, which is the merge commit for the context-budget bundle and therefore the first commit that carries it through the full matrix. Result: success, all legs. The scheduled run at 06:30Z that failed was on a72725b0, which predates the Windows tracker root-contract fix, so that red is explained by commit rather than by flake and is not a live failure surface.\n\nThe pattern worth keeping on this item: a scheduled nightly failure and a dispatched nightly success on the same day are not a contradiction when the schedule fired on an older commit. Reading the head SHA of the failing run before triaging the failure is the cheapest way to avoid re-investigating a fix that already landed. Two consecutive passes have now resolved a nightly red this way."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-30T09:21:18.633Z","harness:claude-code","Nightly verdict recorded 2026-07-30. The 06:30Z scheduled run 30519801227 was RED on exactly one leg (windows-latest, Node 24) and exactly one spec: tests/unit/core/store/item-store-root-contract.spec.ts > item metadata tracker-root contract > rejects a regular file root with a stable typed diagnostic. Test Files 1 failed / 396 passed. That run started at 06:30Z; PR 823, which fixes precisely that contract by inspecting existing ancestors after ENOENT, merged at 08:52Z. So the red window was pre-fix, not a HEAD regression.\n\nVerified by dispatch rather than by inference: workflow_dispatch run 30529480380 on main is GREEN on all five legs (ubuntu Node 22, ubuntu Node 24, ubuntu Node 25, macos Node 24, windows Node 24). HEAD is clean on the Windows leg.\n\nResidual worth noting for this item's scope: the same nightly log shows two MCP contract-violation warnings emitted by our own integration suite and failing nothing - Unknown option \"full\" for pm_update action \"update\" and Unknown option \"dryRun\" for pm_run action \"test-all\". Neither option is declared by the CLI either (pm update has no --full, pm test-all has no --dry-run), so these are suite-side arguments that no contract knows. The warning fires on every nightly and no gate escalates it."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T18:28:09.090Z","harness:codex",Cross-platform conformance should preserve the semantic case on supporting platforms and condition only the platform-inexpressible fixture; treating an unsupported Unix socket fixture as a Windows product failure destroys nightly signal.
